1
00:00:00,216 --> 00:00:01,216
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,216 --> 00:00:02,216
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,216 --> 00:00:03,289
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,289 --> 00:00:05,516
[2018 South Korea vs. Germany match]

5
00:00:05,516 --> 00:00:08,049
Republic of Korea!

6
00:00:09,036 --> 00:00:10,749
Republic of Korea!

7
00:00:10,749 --> 00:00:12,483
[Korea, toward victory]

8
00:00:12,483 --> 00:00:14,716
[Korea! Let the victory chants ring out!]
Republic of Korea!

9
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:16,849
[Episode 7]

10
00:00:16,849 --> 00:00:21,349
Pickpockets taking advantage
of the World Cup crowds in the square!

11
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:24,383
Pickpocket! Pickpocket!

12
00:00:26,724 --> 00:00:30,244
I do like soccer,
but I'm really not here to have fun.

13
00:00:30,244 --> 00:00:31,480
Who knows?

14
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:34,049
Maybe I'll even get a shot
for a police sketch, huh?

15
00:00:37,512 --> 00:00:41,349
I've got the bait set up
absolutely perfectly.

16
00:00:44,308 --> 00:00:45,483
I'm hanging up.

17
00:00:45,483 --> 00:00:49,116
Hey, you in the red cap, stop!

18
00:00:51,948 --> 00:00:53,716
That one is a fake.

19
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:57,483
The real one, loaded with cash, is this.

20
00:00:58,490 --> 00:01:00,190
Darn it!

21
00:01:02,996 --> 00:01:05,248
Darn it!

22
00:01:05,248 --> 00:01:09,016
If you don't want your picture taken,
at least give me an interview!

23
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:13,488
The old man told me
to keep a low profile for a while.

24
00:01:13,488 --> 00:01:15,804
You know I always listen to my backer.

25
00:01:15,804 --> 00:01:19,764
<i>Hey, I heard that dead delivery guy
was a widower with kids.</i>

26
00:01:19,764 --> 00:01:22,948
<i>Man, of all people, you had to hit
a guy like that with your car?</i>

27
00:01:22,948 --> 00:01:25,048
Hey, what on earth are you talking about?

28
00:01:25,048 --> 00:01:29,264
The whole front end of
my 300-million-won babe got wrecked.

29
00:01:29,264 --> 00:01:30,900
I'm the victim here.

30
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:33,524
<i>Hey, we scored! We scored!</i>

31
00:01:33,524 --> 00:01:36,088
Jeez, so what?

32
00:01:36,088 --> 00:01:37,788
Hello?

33
00:01:41,228 --> 00:01:45,716
Oh, my, these darn things
are pissing me off so much.

34
00:01:46,644 --> 00:01:50,349
Oh, it's Dumbass Korea, you punks!

35
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:22,680
Meeting concluded.

36
00:02:24,207 --> 00:02:25,907
<i>Is it over?</i>

37
00:02:27,808 --> 00:02:29,704
It's finally over.

38
00:02:29,704 --> 00:02:31,244
Relax, rookie.

39
00:02:31,244 --> 00:02:33,216
Get that cramp out of your leg too.

40
00:02:33,216 --> 00:02:36,216
Pardon? I wasn't nervous or anything...

41
00:02:41,916 --> 00:02:44,516
Half of a meeting is just waiting.

42
00:02:45,228 --> 00:02:46,868
So what does that require?

43
00:02:46,868 --> 00:02:48,968
Endurance.

44
00:02:48,968 --> 00:02:51,428
I should work on my strength.

45
00:02:51,428 --> 00:02:53,449
Good work, Ms. Yoo.

46
00:02:55,262 --> 00:02:58,124
You did a pretty good job too.

47
00:02:58,124 --> 00:02:59,832
I can leave with peace of mind.

48
00:02:59,832 --> 00:03:01,296
What?

49
00:03:01,296 --> 00:03:03,832
Leave? Where? Who's leaving?

50
00:03:03,832 --> 00:03:06,883
Excellent work for your first meeting.
Good job.

51
00:03:09,112 --> 00:03:11,312
Take the emergency stairs down
to the first floor.

52
00:03:11,312 --> 00:03:14,548
Exit through Gate 3 and blend into the crowd.

53
00:03:14,548 --> 00:03:16,248
Okay.

54
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:21,932
But you can't watch the soccer match.
What are you going to do?

55
00:03:21,932 --> 00:03:23,468
<i>I'm not interested.</i>

56
00:03:23,468 --> 00:03:25,483
Really? That's unusual.

57
00:03:25,483 --> 00:03:27,468
<i>You're not interested either.</i>

58
00:03:27,468 --> 00:03:29,808
That's why you scheduled
a meeting on a day like this.

59
00:03:29,808 --> 00:03:33,383
Hey, that's because today is
a good day to hold a meeting.

60
00:03:34,852 --> 00:03:36,148
But, Ms. Yoo,

61
00:03:36,148 --> 00:03:41,216
do you have any interest in
anything besides work?

62
00:03:48,192 --> 00:03:50,884
Have you picked up any movement right now?

63
00:03:50,884 --> 00:03:52,214
Around the emergency stairs.

64
00:03:52,214 --> 00:03:53,914
<i>Pardon?</i>

65
00:03:57,660 --> 00:03:58,660
No.

66
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:01,808
Other than the security office,
the whole building is empty.

67
00:04:01,808 --> 00:04:04,172
Then rewind and see if we missed anything.

68
00:04:04,172 --> 00:04:05,544
Since I came upstairs.

69
00:04:05,544 --> 00:04:06,952
Is something wrong?

70
00:04:06,952 --> 00:04:08,652
Let me know if you find something.

71
00:04:37,549 --> 00:04:40,916
[Kwon Tae Seong]

72
00:04:46,083 --> 00:04:49,483
[Not Today Reporter, Kwon Tae Seong]

73
00:04:56,247 --> 00:04:58,849
[Gate 3]

74
00:05:00,016 --> 00:05:01,556
[Emergency Stairs]

75
00:05:01,556 --> 00:05:02,956
Ms. Yoo.

76
00:05:02,956 --> 00:05:06,372
About ten minutes ago,
two men ran in through Gate 3.

77
00:05:06,372 --> 00:05:08,872
It looked like they were chasing each other.

78
00:05:08,872 --> 00:05:11,712
They went into the emergency stairwell
one after another.

79
00:05:11,712 --> 00:05:15,183
Five minutes later,
only the first man came back out.

80
00:05:16,296 --> 00:05:18,092
I missed them.

81
00:05:18,092 --> 00:05:19,284
I'm sorry, Ms. Yoo.

82
00:05:19,284 --> 00:05:22,508
Okay. Keep watching.

83
00:05:22,508 --> 00:05:24,208
But what...

84
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:29,483
You should be more careful.

85
00:05:35,249 --> 00:05:37,049
[Emergency Call]

86
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:41,236
Yes, someone has collapsed and is bleeding
from the head on the fifth floor

87
00:05:41,236 --> 00:05:43,592
of the emergency stairs at King Tower.

88
00:05:43,592 --> 00:05:45,816
I think he's going to die
if you don't get here quickly.

89
00:06:01,232 --> 00:06:02,616
Try to stay alive if you can.

90
00:06:02,616 --> 00:06:05,104
Looks like they won the soccer game too.

91
00:06:05,104 --> 00:06:07,549
One victim is enough for today.

92
00:06:13,916 --> 00:06:16,183
[Four Months Later]

93
00:06:16,183 --> 00:06:17,183
[Kwon Tae Seong]
Let me see.

94
00:06:17,183 --> 00:06:18,592
Ugh, what?

95
00:06:18,592 --> 00:06:19,692
Hold still.

96
00:06:19,692 --> 00:06:20,944
- Wait, what is it?
- Let me see.

97
00:06:20,944 --> 00:06:23,549
Oh, come on. What is it?

98
00:06:27,076 --> 00:06:28,784
Looks like your head's still attached.

99
00:06:28,784 --> 00:06:30,883
Are you insane?

100
00:06:31,632 --> 00:06:34,796
Oh, right, I can walk starting today.

101
00:06:34,796 --> 00:06:36,916
Hey, hey, hey! Hey!

102
00:06:39,349 --> 00:06:40,349
It feels weird.

103
00:06:40,349 --> 00:06:42,484
If you saw a pickpocket,
you should've called the police.

104
00:06:42,484 --> 00:06:44,083
Why did you chase him, you punk?

105
00:06:44,083 --> 00:06:46,416
I think I've got a cramp.

106
00:06:47,264 --> 00:06:49,620
How do you give me the same lecture
every time you visit?

107
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:50,896
Impressive, really.

108
00:06:50,896 --> 00:06:54,008
Ugh, I've heard it enough already.

109
00:06:54,008 --> 00:06:55,928
You think this is funny?
You feel like laughing right now?

110
00:06:55,928 --> 00:06:58,364
You just woke up after four months,
you crazy punk.

111
00:06:58,364 --> 00:07:01,283
How could you call someone
with a head injury "crazy"?

112
00:07:04,208 --> 00:07:05,308
Oh, right!

113
00:07:05,308 --> 00:07:07,128
You still haven't caught the guy
who hit me from behind, right?

114
00:07:07,128 --> 00:07:09,684
Don't go trying to catch him yourself.

115
00:07:09,684 --> 00:07:11,148
Why?

116
00:07:11,148 --> 00:07:12,812
Because I think you'd actually kill him
if you caught him.

117
00:07:12,812 --> 00:07:14,176
Of course, I would. Completely.

118
00:07:14,176 --> 00:07:15,883
You really...

119
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:20,920
Hey!

120
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,676
Did you even know the rooftop

121
00:07:22,676 --> 00:07:24,960
where you collapsed
was the Kingfisher sniper's position?

122
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:27,676
Exactly. Oh! What a darn waste.

123
00:07:27,676 --> 00:07:31,164
If I hadn't cracked my head,
I could've met Kingfisher.

124
00:07:31,164 --> 00:07:32,712
You probably would've.

125
00:07:32,712 --> 00:07:36,008
Instead, you would've had
a hole in your head, you punk.

126
00:07:36,008 --> 00:07:38,316
That's defamatory toward Kingfisher.

127
00:07:38,316 --> 00:07:41,783
Why? Because I'm an innocent citizen.

128
00:07:43,028 --> 00:07:46,628
I can't tell if you are lucky or unlucky...

129
00:07:46,628 --> 00:07:50,249
I'm really anxious about
what kind of woman will take you away.

130
00:08:13,288 --> 00:08:16,088
Manager Yoo, you don't have to
come by so often. I feel bad about it.

131
00:08:16,088 --> 00:08:18,304
It's not like being sick
is anything to brag about.

132
00:08:18,304 --> 00:08:20,683
You got hurt doing your job.

133
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:22,964
How are you feeling?

134
00:08:22,964 --> 00:08:26,804
Maybe it's because I'm getting older.
Even my bones aren't healing properly.

135
00:08:26,804 --> 00:08:29,440
Oh, you've all been through a lot
because of me, right?

136
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:31,512
Everyone's worried about you.

137
00:08:31,512 --> 00:08:34,296
You know you need to be careful about
complications after a traffic accident?

138
00:08:34,296 --> 00:08:36,283
Then this...

139
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,648
Darn it.

140
00:08:38,648 --> 00:08:40,348
This is good.

141
00:08:46,356 --> 00:08:48,416
- This?
- Yeah.

142
00:08:55,212 --> 00:08:56,960
Oh, by the way,

143
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,483
I hear the rookie is pretty capable.

144
00:08:59,483 --> 00:09:01,900
Yeah, after Assistant Manager Son quit,

145
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:04,616
I was worried about
how to fill such a big vacancy.

146
00:09:04,616 --> 00:09:07,936
But now I can breathe easier.

147
00:09:07,936 --> 00:09:09,912
The vacancy you left
is even bigger, Director.

148
00:09:09,912 --> 00:09:11,840
Please get well and come back soon.

149
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:15,583
I can't leave in peace until you're back.

150
00:09:17,352 --> 00:09:20,484
Manager Yoo, have you made up your mind?

151
00:09:20,484 --> 00:09:23,984
Are you really going to quit?

152
00:09:23,984 --> 00:09:26,083
I think I'm just tired.

153
00:09:26,083 --> 00:09:28,392
Yeah. I can understand that.

154
00:09:28,392 --> 00:09:34,188
They say even ordinary people
can burn out after working for ten years.

155
00:09:34,188 --> 00:09:39,340
You've been working nonstop.
No wonder you're exhausted.

156
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:41,040
Right?

157
00:09:42,444 --> 00:09:45,516
And this isn't exactly
an ordinary line of work, right?

158
00:09:45,516 --> 00:09:49,160
It's endless, no matter how much you do.

159
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:52,224
And the world stays exactly the same.

160
00:09:52,224 --> 00:09:56,516
I understand how you feel.

161
00:09:56,516 --> 00:09:58,249
Manager Yoo.

162
00:09:58,964 --> 00:10:01,476
Could you reconsider it one more time?

163
00:10:01,476 --> 00:10:04,649
For now, stay off on-site meetings.

164
00:10:04,649 --> 00:10:08,960
Just take it easy, okay?

165
00:10:30,348 --> 00:10:34,883
[10 Lifestyle Tips for Cancer Prevention]

166
00:10:49,917 --> 00:10:51,617
Just a moment!

167
00:10:54,288 --> 00:10:56,249
Come down. Hurry.

168
00:11:00,864 --> 00:11:03,216
Come on, slow down!

169
00:11:04,644 --> 00:11:06,928
Why?

170
00:11:06,928 --> 00:11:10,400
Huh? "Why?"

171
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:12,100
Oh, why...

172
00:11:13,397 --> 00:11:15,449
Because life is precious?

173
00:11:16,604 --> 00:11:18,683
What I'm trying to say is,

174
00:11:18,683 --> 00:11:21,749
after nearly dying recently,
I realized a few things.

175
00:11:21,749 --> 00:11:23,428
I mean...

176
00:11:23,428 --> 00:11:27,449
Just looking at the sky,
watching the leaves change.

177
00:11:27,449 --> 00:11:29,683
"Wow, I'm glad I'm alive."

178
00:11:30,401 --> 00:11:32,583
"It's good to be alive."

179
00:11:32,583 --> 00:11:37,784
Joking around with friends,
getting nagged by your family...

180
00:11:37,784 --> 00:11:39,252
Worrying about silly things like,

181
00:11:39,252 --> 00:11:41,805
"What should I eat today?"
or "What should I wear tomorrow?"

182
00:11:41,805 --> 00:11:46,149
That ordinary everyday life is so precious.
It really is precious.

183
00:11:46,149 --> 00:11:47,916
So...

184
00:11:50,512 --> 00:11:53,683
I hope you live and don't die.

185
00:12:31,309 --> 00:12:33,703
Says life is precious,
yet here you are smoking,

186
00:12:33,703 --> 00:12:35,283
especially after you nearly died?

187
00:12:35,283 --> 00:12:36,628
Isn't that a little much?

188
00:12:36,628 --> 00:12:39,583
This isn't mine.
I just found it on my way here...

189
00:12:42,356 --> 00:12:43,878
Take care.

190
00:12:43,878 --> 00:12:46,549
Enjoy your ordinary life, one day at a time.

191
00:12:47,404 --> 00:12:49,183
Excuse me!

192
00:12:51,583 --> 00:12:54,283
Have we met before?

193
00:12:57,472 --> 00:12:58,788
No.

194
00:12:58,788 --> 00:13:00,582
I'm sure I've seen you before.

195
00:13:00,582 --> 00:13:02,616
Even your voice sounds familiar.

196
00:13:04,462 --> 00:13:07,411
Oh, I'm sorry. I...

197
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:11,144
I injured my head,
so I think I'm a little out of it.

198
00:13:11,144 --> 00:13:15,283
I'm sure my memory will come back
once I fully recover, right?

199
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:18,149
<i>"Kwon Tae Seong."</i>

200
00:13:18,149 --> 00:13:19,916
[Not Today Social Affairs Reporter]
He works for an online news outlet.

201
00:13:19,916 --> 00:13:22,884
I looked through some of his past articles.

202
00:13:22,884 --> 00:13:24,008
[Supporting the vulnerable]
His focus is on social justice

203
00:13:24,008 --> 00:13:25,408
[isn't a privilege, but a choice]
and protecting the vulnerable.

204
00:13:25,408 --> 00:13:27,365
He's a pretty rare type
of reporter these days.

205
00:13:27,365 --> 00:13:29,556
But why him?

206
00:13:29,556 --> 00:13:31,720
Just in case, for precaution. Keep going.

207
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,416
Is this why you're interested in him?

208
00:13:33,416 --> 00:13:34,483
[Kingfisher]

209
00:13:34,483 --> 00:13:38,616
Every article about Kingfisher
in this outlet was written by him.

210
00:13:38,616 --> 00:13:40,521
I skimmed through them.

211
00:13:40,521 --> 00:13:41,685
He doesn't really

212
00:13:41,685 --> 00:13:43,108
[Kingfisher: Notorious Killer]
take a negative stance on Kingfisher.

213
00:13:43,108 --> 00:13:44,111
[or Avenger of Justice?]
He's more focused on

214
00:13:44,111 --> 00:13:45,672
analyzing the phenomenon
than just following the cases.

215
00:13:45,672 --> 00:13:50,116
Apparently, both the industry and readers
consider his articles fairly insightful.

216
00:13:50,116 --> 00:13:53,816
Oh, and he has a personal blog too.

217
00:13:53,816 --> 00:13:56,496
Send me the link,
along with the article right now.

218
00:13:56,496 --> 00:13:58,196
All of it?

219
00:13:59,949 --> 00:14:03,883
She normally doesn't even
care about the articles...

220
00:14:10,532 --> 00:14:13,567
<i>"Kingfisher: Notorious Killer
or Avenger of Justice?"</i>

221
00:14:13,567 --> 00:14:15,117
<i>"The Painful Questions Kingfisher
Forces Our Society to Ask."</i>

222
00:14:15,117 --> 00:14:17,044
<i>"Five Reflections on Kingfisher."</i>

223
00:14:17,044 --> 00:14:19,836
<i>"Can We Really Trust Our Justice System?"</i>

224
00:14:19,836 --> 00:14:22,649
<i>"If I Ever Meet Kingfisher."</i>

225
00:14:22,649 --> 00:14:26,391
<i>Luckily, I grew up smoothly
in the care of a close-knit family,</i>

226
00:14:26,391 --> 00:14:30,252
<i>and I was a pretty ordinary,
well-behaved student throughout school.</i>

227
00:14:30,252 --> 00:14:32,424
How about best of three?
Loser pays for the pizza.

228
00:14:32,424 --> 00:14:34,884
Don't be a sore loser if you lose, huh?

229
00:14:34,884 --> 00:14:36,684
You'd better not lose
and start crying, you punk.

230
00:14:36,684 --> 00:14:38,316
Hey, how many times have you lost already?

231
00:14:38,316 --> 00:14:40,116
Oh, forget it.

232
00:14:59,056 --> 00:15:02,332
<i>If it weren't for a tragic incident
that happened to a friend one day,</i>

233
00:15:02,332 --> 00:15:06,776
<i>I might have lived a life
distant from crime and illegality.</i>

234
00:15:06,776 --> 00:15:11,248
<i>A sniper shooting occurred
in the heart of Seoul.</i>

235
00:15:11,248 --> 00:15:12,248
<i>According to police,</i>

236
00:15:12,248 --> 00:15:13,249
- <i>at an officetel in Semyung-dong,</i>
- A gun?

237
00:15:13,249 --> 00:15:15,560
- <i>a man in his 40s was shot...</i>
- Look at that.

238
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:19,480
<i>I still remember the shock
of first hearing about him.</i>

239
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:22,283
<i>Someone out there picks out
only the cruel, ruthless criminals</i>

240
00:15:22,283 --> 00:15:25,424
<i>who crush the everyday lives
of decent people and eliminates them?</i>

241
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:28,615
Honestly, isn't Kingfisher kind of cool?

242
00:15:28,615 --> 00:15:30,680
What's cool about him?
He's just a psycho killer.

243
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,681
Hey, but he only picks
and kills the bad guys.

244
00:15:33,681 --> 00:15:38,416
Even if he only kills bad people,
a killer is still a killer.

245
00:15:38,416 --> 00:15:43,374
<i>While the world was divided in its opinions,
I couldn't help wondering.</i>

246
00:15:43,374 --> 00:15:45,016
<i>What kind of person</i>

247
00:15:45,016 --> 00:15:48,316
<i>would devote their entire life
to something like that?</i>

248
00:15:55,216 --> 00:15:56,999
[Reporter Attacked While Covering Pickpockets
Wakes Up After Four Months]

249
00:15:56,999 --> 00:15:58,351
Reporter Kwon, on the day of the incident...

250
00:15:59,549 --> 00:16:02,482
[Rooftop Where Reporter Kwon Collapsed
Revealed as Kingfisher's Sniper's Nest]

251
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,888
<i>Have we met before?</i>

252
00:16:33,888 --> 00:16:38,316
I'm sure my memory will come back
once I fully recover, right?

253
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:02,168
I don't think you made this yourself.

254
00:17:02,168 --> 00:17:03,168
I made it myself.

255
00:17:03,168 --> 00:17:06,149
- You bought this?
- No, I made it.

256
00:17:07,096 --> 00:17:08,096
How is it?

257
00:17:08,096 --> 00:17:10,264
- You bought this?
- No, it's not!

258
00:17:10,264 --> 00:17:12,364
I really made it. I really did.

259
00:17:12,364 --> 00:17:14,416
I really made it.

260
00:17:16,188 --> 00:17:18,424
How is it?

261
00:17:18,424 --> 00:17:19,496
It's good.

262
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:21,016
Is that it?

263
00:17:21,016 --> 00:17:23,049
What more do you want? I said it's good.

264
00:17:23,049 --> 00:17:25,583
I made it, and I did a good job.

265
00:17:30,096 --> 00:17:32,083
Miss! Excuse me, just a moment!

266
00:17:32,808 --> 00:17:35,416
Wow, I finally found you.

267
00:17:35,416 --> 00:17:37,988
I've been waiting for you.

268
00:17:37,988 --> 00:17:39,583
Why?

269
00:17:39,583 --> 00:17:42,616
I remembered where we met.

270
00:17:44,768 --> 00:17:46,949
You lived in Hoewon-dong
when you were little, right?

271
00:17:48,552 --> 00:17:50,583
No, I've never lived there.

272
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:54,752
You went to Jeongin Middle School, right?

273
00:17:54,752 --> 00:17:56,452
No.

274
00:17:58,916 --> 00:18:00,180
Did you ever attend Bright Shine Academy...

275
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:01,880
No.

276
00:18:05,392 --> 00:18:08,648
Has anyone ever told you that
you look like actress Choi So Hyun...

277
00:18:08,648 --> 00:18:10,972
No, right?

278
00:18:12,212 --> 00:18:13,404
I'm sorry.

279
00:18:13,404 --> 00:18:16,976
I'll think harder

280
00:18:16,976 --> 00:18:20,683
and try to figure it out next time.

281
00:18:27,104 --> 00:18:31,248
Oh, you might think
I'm trying to hit on you or something,

282
00:18:31,248 --> 00:18:32,964
but I'm absolutely not. Absolutely not.

283
00:18:32,964 --> 00:18:34,783
If we happen to run into each other again...

284
00:18:34,783 --> 00:18:36,752
No, that won't happen.

285
00:18:36,752 --> 00:18:39,296
Don't waste your time.

286
00:18:39,296 --> 00:18:41,636
We've never met.

287
00:18:41,636 --> 00:18:43,336
Wait...

288
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:47,149
She's got no mercy.

289
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:52,116
Oh, I should have asked her name.

290
00:19:00,428 --> 00:19:02,088
<i>Are you having trouble sleeping?</i>

291
00:19:02,088 --> 00:19:03,656
<i>Even when you fall asleep, you wake up soon,</i>

292
00:19:03,656 --> 00:19:05,849
and you sometimes have nightmares, right?

293
00:19:05,849 --> 00:19:06,884
Yeah, well...

294
00:19:06,884 --> 00:19:10,449
Have you experienced
any major stress recently?

295
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:19,649
Problems in your relationships,
or pressure at work?

296
00:19:22,383 --> 00:19:24,183
No, nothing.

297
00:19:24,183 --> 00:19:26,405
Still nothing, huh?

298
00:19:26,405 --> 00:19:27,688
All right.

299
00:19:27,688 --> 00:19:31,192
I can increase the dosage
of your sleeping pills,

300
00:19:31,192 --> 00:19:32,892
but I think...

301
00:19:39,148 --> 00:19:42,849
You're pretty good. Is it fun?

302
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:50,068
Oh, really?

303
00:19:50,068 --> 00:19:51,616
Want to go watch it later?

304
00:19:51,616 --> 00:19:53,449
- No, we can't.
- Ah.

305
00:19:53,449 --> 00:19:56,316
No, here it is!

306
00:20:01,349 --> 00:20:04,656
[Sales Team 3 Team Leader, Bae Yun Ok]

307
00:20:04,656 --> 00:20:07,036
[Resignation Letter]
I hereby resign.

308
00:20:07,036 --> 00:20:09,383
Please accept my resignation,
Team Leader Bae.

309
00:20:35,452 --> 00:20:38,016
Here they come. Here they come.

310
00:20:38,016 --> 00:20:40,024
Here they come!

311
00:20:40,024 --> 00:20:42,332
Have you figured out how the two men
ended up getting hit by the same shot?

312
00:20:42,332 --> 00:20:44,549
Could the target have been only one person,
with Kingfisher accidentally...

313
00:20:44,549 --> 00:20:46,624
We're not cops.
We're just employees out for a meal.

314
00:20:46,624 --> 00:20:47,624
- Yeah.
- He says he's not a cop.

315
00:20:47,624 --> 00:20:50,083
- He's not a cop?
- What?

316
00:20:52,916 --> 00:20:54,236
You're a pretty good liar, aren't you?

317
00:20:54,236 --> 00:20:56,388
Hey, half of it was true.

318
00:20:56,388 --> 00:20:58,316
It's true we're not the local police here.

319
00:20:58,316 --> 00:21:00,004
I'm so hungry I'm about to pass out.

320
00:21:00,004 --> 00:21:02,120
All I ate last night was two chocolate pies.

321
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:04,052
I had one cream bun.

322
00:21:04,052 --> 00:21:05,752
Oh...

323
00:21:06,408 --> 00:21:10,536
Wow, looks like the one-shot double kill
really is the hottest topic.

324
00:21:10,536 --> 00:21:13,044
It's the first case like this in 16 years.

325
00:21:13,044 --> 00:21:15,096
And the internet is going crazy over it.

326
00:21:15,096 --> 00:21:16,908
The original target was just Tak Jong Gu.

327
00:21:16,908 --> 00:21:18,932
Kingfisher was trying to shoot him
and accidentally killed someone else.

328
00:21:18,932 --> 00:21:22,149
Do you really think Kingfisher is
the kind of guy who'd make a mistake?

329
00:21:22,149 --> 00:21:23,904
No way. He'd never do that!

330
00:21:23,904 --> 00:21:26,156
Anyway, let's say Tak Jong Gu is one thing,

331
00:21:26,156 --> 00:21:28,904
but that Cheon... whatever his name is,
what's the chairman's charge?

332
00:21:28,904 --> 00:21:30,776
That's what we're about to find out.

333
00:21:30,776 --> 00:21:33,756
Why Cheon Seong Gil became a target.

334
00:21:33,756 --> 00:21:36,396
Right now? Without even eating first?

335
00:21:36,396 --> 00:21:39,412
Sir, I only had two chocolate pies... Sir!

336
00:21:39,412 --> 00:21:42,904
<i>This case is unusual not only
because there are two victims,</i>

337
00:21:42,904 --> 00:21:47,096
<i>but also because the criminal history
of one of them hasn't been confirmed yet.</i>

338
00:21:47,096 --> 00:21:49,377
<i>So, the question is whether Kingfisher</i>

339
00:21:49,377 --> 00:21:51,883
<i>may have accidentally killed
an innocent person...</i>

340
00:21:51,883 --> 00:21:55,432
<i>If that turns out to be true,
public opinion could shift dramatically.</i>

341
00:21:55,432 --> 00:21:58,232
<i>Until now, he was believed
to only kill serious criminals...</i>

342
00:21:58,232 --> 00:21:59,232
Yes, Ms. Gu.

343
00:21:59,232 --> 00:22:00,884
[Reporter Gu Hae Na]
<i>Mr. Kwon, where are you now?</i>

344
00:22:00,884 --> 00:22:02,776
We've heard from someone
with information on Cheon Seong Gil.

345
00:22:02,776 --> 00:22:04,812
They've agreed to an interview.

346
00:22:04,812 --> 00:22:07,249
<i>We're meeting them right now.</i>

347
00:22:08,172 --> 00:22:09,836
<i>Hello?</i>

348
00:22:09,836 --> 00:22:13,504
Mr. Kwon? Are you listening?

349
00:22:13,504 --> 00:22:15,749
Where are you meeting them?

350
00:22:21,892 --> 00:22:23,483
Mother, I'm here.

351
00:22:23,483 --> 00:22:24,828
Oh, welcome...

352
00:22:24,828 --> 00:22:27,688
Bo Na, what brings you here at this hour?
Didn't you go to work?

353
00:22:27,688 --> 00:22:31,204
Well, my business trip ended a day early,
so I don't have to go in today.

354
00:22:31,204 --> 00:22:34,480
And I brought something for you, Mother.

355
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:37,649
Huh? What is it?

356
00:22:38,648 --> 00:22:41,188
I thought you might be
having trouble sleeping lately

357
00:22:41,188 --> 00:22:44,004
and getting hot flashes, so I was worried.

358
00:22:44,004 --> 00:22:47,648
I've indeed been a bit hot
under the collar lately.

359
00:22:47,648 --> 00:22:50,484
But I wonder why that is?

360
00:22:50,484 --> 00:22:53,128
Mother, they say
that's all part of menopause.

361
00:22:53,128 --> 00:22:55,949
But if you take one packet a day,
it helps manage...

362
00:22:55,949 --> 00:22:58,080
Oh, jeez.

363
00:22:58,080 --> 00:23:00,083
Well, is there anything I can help with?

364
00:23:00,083 --> 00:23:01,528
What could you possibly help with?

365
00:23:01,528 --> 00:23:03,636
You must be tired from your business trip.
Go home and get some rest.

366
00:23:03,636 --> 00:23:05,400
No, I'm fine.

367
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:07,172
It's not like anyone's provoking me.

368
00:23:07,172 --> 00:23:09,668
Hey, if you have eyes, just look around.

369
00:23:09,668 --> 00:23:11,644
Do you see anything that needs helping with?

370
00:23:11,644 --> 00:23:13,012
Oh, dear.

371
00:23:13,012 --> 00:23:14,984
Even if there were something to do,

372
00:23:14,984 --> 00:23:16,996
would I feel comfortable asking you to do it?

373
00:23:16,996 --> 00:23:19,972
If I push my precious
daughter-in-law too hard,

374
00:23:19,972 --> 00:23:23,244
I'll get an earful from my son again.

375
00:23:23,244 --> 00:23:26,624
Mom, why are you taking it out on her?

376
00:23:26,624 --> 00:23:29,716
She's just cranky because business is slow.

377
00:23:30,683 --> 00:23:31,808
Mother.

378
00:23:31,808 --> 00:23:35,012
This can help with mood swings
during menopause too!

379
00:23:35,012 --> 00:23:36,879
Yeah, Mom. Want me to open it for you?

380
00:23:36,879 --> 00:23:39,112
What...

381
00:23:39,112 --> 00:23:41,316
Oh, welcome!

382
00:23:42,383 --> 00:23:45,296
- Hello.
- Oh, my, welcome.

383
00:23:45,296 --> 00:23:46,964
- Have a seat here.
- Welcome.

384
00:23:46,964 --> 00:23:48,816
Oh, Mr. Kim, what brings you here?

385
00:23:48,816 --> 00:23:52,352
I came by for lunch after the neighborhood
merchant association meeting.

386
00:23:52,352 --> 00:23:54,128
Oh, my, thank you.

387
00:23:54,128 --> 00:23:56,952
About twenty more people
will be coming later.

388
00:23:56,952 --> 00:24:00,949
The director of the senior center next door
was looking for a good chicken shop,

389
00:24:00,949 --> 00:24:02,676
so I recommended yours.

390
00:24:02,676 --> 00:24:04,888
Oh, my goodness.

391
00:24:04,888 --> 00:24:07,700
Oh, my, Mr. Kim, you're such a lifesaver.

392
00:24:07,700 --> 00:24:08,983
Just give us a moment.

393
00:24:08,983 --> 00:24:11,783
- We'll make it delicious.
- Everyone, please order.

394
00:24:13,572 --> 00:24:16,283
Hello, this is Tae Seong Chicken.

395
00:24:16,283 --> 00:24:18,192
Pardon? The children's welfare center?

396
00:24:18,192 --> 00:24:20,092
Yes, I know it.

397
00:24:20,092 --> 00:24:21,412
Yes.

398
00:24:21,412 --> 00:24:23,668
What? Twenty chickens?

399
00:24:23,668 --> 00:24:25,676
By five o'clock?

400
00:24:25,676 --> 00:24:28,708
Yes, we'll make them deliciously
and send them over.

401
00:24:28,708 --> 00:24:30,056
Okay.

402
00:24:30,056 --> 00:24:31,384
Twenty chickens?

403
00:24:31,384 --> 00:24:33,168
- Yeah.
- What's going on?

404
00:24:33,168 --> 00:24:35,212
What do you mean, "what's going on"?
It's a lucky day.

405
00:24:35,212 --> 00:24:37,704
- Start frying the chicken.
- Got it.

406
00:24:37,704 --> 00:24:41,036
We're in trouble.
We've got our hands full now.

407
00:24:41,036 --> 00:24:42,736
I'm right here...

408
00:24:43,460 --> 00:24:46,416
Yul's mommy, are you still here?

409
00:24:47,176 --> 00:24:49,116
Mother, I'm here.

410
00:24:50,016 --> 00:24:51,140
Thank you.

411
00:24:51,140 --> 00:24:52,860
- Take care going home. Alright.
- Thank you!

412
00:24:52,860 --> 00:24:54,583
Take care.

413
00:24:59,572 --> 00:25:01,736
This worked out perfectly, didn't it?

414
00:25:01,736 --> 00:25:04,716
I wondered how we could write a story
without any witnesses or evidence.

415
00:25:04,716 --> 00:25:07,536
It couldn't have been easy,
but they found the courage to come forward.

416
00:25:07,536 --> 00:25:10,849
Jeez, what, innocent lives?

417
00:25:10,849 --> 00:25:14,316
They have no idea
how evil Cheon Seong Gil was.

418
00:25:14,932 --> 00:25:16,632
Let's go.

419
00:25:19,396 --> 00:25:22,648
But, Mr. Kwon, your intuition is amazing.

420
00:25:22,648 --> 00:25:24,856
Like with Pyo Kyu Cheol last time,

421
00:25:24,856 --> 00:25:29,188
how do you keep picking out exactly
the people Kingfisher targets?

422
00:25:29,188 --> 00:25:34,912
At this rate, aren't we going to
run into Kingfisher somewhere?

423
00:25:34,912 --> 00:25:38,349
Maybe we've already crossed paths
without even knowing it, right?

424
00:25:38,976 --> 00:25:42,372
Aren't you scared? Who knows
what will happen once Kingfisher shows up?

425
00:25:42,372 --> 00:25:43,560
What?

426
00:25:43,560 --> 00:25:48,732
Oh, come on. I'm just an innocent citizen.

427
00:25:48,732 --> 00:25:50,432
Let's go, Mr. Kwon.

428
00:25:53,432 --> 00:25:55,049
It's hot, so be careful.

429
00:25:55,049 --> 00:25:56,484
- Ma'am, one more fried chicken, please.
- Yes.

430
00:25:56,484 --> 00:25:58,860
Okay, one fried chicken.
Sun Il, one more fried chicken!

431
00:25:58,860 --> 00:26:00,080
- Oh, got it.
- Yeah.

432
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:01,636
- And one Coke, please.
- Want a Coke?

433
00:26:01,636 --> 00:26:02,824
Oh, I'll get it.

434
00:26:02,824 --> 00:26:05,444
- Take these to the empty tables.
- Yeah, Mother.

435
00:26:05,444 --> 00:26:06,728
Want some more pickled radish?

436
00:26:06,728 --> 00:26:08,308
Here, your Coke.

437
00:26:08,308 --> 00:26:09,876
Want more sauce?

438
00:26:09,876 --> 00:26:10,949
The drumstick is mine.

439
00:26:10,949 --> 00:26:13,149
I'll give you a cider on the house.

440
00:26:13,149 --> 00:26:14,420
[Mr. Kim Gil Dong,
Real Estate Business Owner]

441
00:26:14,420 --> 00:26:17,504
<i>We'll make good use of the donation
you sent to the merchants' association.</i>

442
00:26:17,504 --> 00:26:19,589
[Tae Seong Chicken]
<i>It would have been great to publicize it</i>

443
00:26:19,589 --> 00:26:21,404
<i>as a win-win effort with our tenants,</i>

444
00:26:21,404 --> 00:26:23,716
<i>but since you asked
to remain anonymous, that's a shame.</i>

445
00:26:23,716 --> 00:26:25,768
[Jung Kyung Hwa]
<i>Thank you for the chicken.</i>

446
00:26:25,768 --> 00:26:27,904
[Director of the Child Welfare Center]
<i>The kids are so excited and waiting for it.</i>

447
00:26:27,904 --> 00:26:29,552
<i>We'll enjoy it.</i>

448
00:26:29,552 --> 00:26:31,252
Thank you.

449
00:26:37,988 --> 00:26:41,240
<i>Attention is once again
turning to Chairman Cheon,</i>

450
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:44,216
<i>who was killed in the shooting
at the casino VIP lounge.</i>

451
00:26:44,216 --> 00:26:47,631
<i>Chairman Cheon, known as
Kingfisher's first civilian victim,</i>

452
00:26:47,631 --> 00:26:48,631
<i>was a respected businessman</i>

453
00:26:48,631 --> 00:26:49,631
[Chairman Cheon]
<i>who made significant contributions</i>

454
00:26:49,631 --> 00:26:51,452
[Renowned Businessman in Gangwon Province]
<i>to Gangwon Province's economy.</i>

455
00:26:51,452 --> 00:26:54,349
- <i>Following Kingfisher's sniper attack...</i>
- I knew it would happen someday.

456
00:26:54,349 --> 00:26:57,644
He was acting all high and mighty,
like a hero or something.

457
00:26:57,644 --> 00:27:00,476
If an innocent person was killed,
he should be held accountable too.

458
00:27:00,476 --> 00:27:02,208
Kingfisher should be caught
and locked up too.

459
00:27:02,208 --> 00:27:04,516
I'll give you the sauced one.
Sun Il, one more sauced chicken here!

460
00:27:04,516 --> 00:27:05,516
- Oh, one sauced chicken.
- Ma'am.

461
00:27:05,516 --> 00:27:06,648
- Yes?
- When will the fried chicken be ready?

462
00:27:06,648 --> 00:27:08,016
The fried chicken?
Sun Il, when is the fried chicken coming out?

463
00:27:08,016 --> 00:27:09,996
- It's out now!
- I'll bring it right out.

464
00:27:09,996 --> 00:27:12,316
<i>Along with the exact circumstances
of Chairman Cheon's death,</i>

465
00:27:12,316 --> 00:27:15,256
<i>the police are also expanding their
investigation into Kingfisher's motives.</i>

466
00:27:15,256 --> 00:27:18,264
What do these people take our Kingfisher for?

467
00:27:18,264 --> 00:27:21,716
What do we do? Director Yoo's going to be
so upset when she hears about this.

468
00:27:21,716 --> 00:27:23,583
Of course, she will.

469
00:27:23,583 --> 00:27:28,249
It's the most important principle
Director Yoo has upheld for 16 years.

470
00:27:28,249 --> 00:27:29,949
[Kingfisher Mistake Controversy,
First Innocent Civilian Sniper Attack?]

471
00:27:34,816 --> 00:27:36,960
I got a text from Director Yoo.

472
00:27:36,960 --> 00:27:38,116
What did she say?

473
00:27:38,116 --> 00:27:39,664
[Reliable Police, A Safe Country]

474
00:27:39,664 --> 00:27:42,516
Hey, get reporters out of the doorway.

475
00:27:43,800 --> 00:27:48,668
Why does that Kingfisher punk
have to come all the way out here...

476
00:27:48,668 --> 00:27:50,368
and cause trouble?

477
00:27:52,616 --> 00:27:54,881
Oh, my, since earlier,

478
00:27:54,881 --> 00:27:56,460
[The Kingfisher Casino Case]
what case have you been digging into?

479
00:27:56,460 --> 00:27:59,464
I heard you went to the scene.

480
00:27:59,464 --> 00:28:04,588
It was obvious the two targets
just happened to be in the same place...

481
00:28:04,588 --> 00:28:06,500
Chairman Cheon has a criminal record.

482
00:28:06,500 --> 00:28:08,864
The sexual assault charge?

483
00:28:08,864 --> 00:28:11,940
Oh, that was a long time ago.

484
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:15,452
What about those workers who died
at his construction site recently?

485
00:28:15,452 --> 00:28:20,908
Those cases were already closed
as accidental falls and suicides.

486
00:28:20,908 --> 00:28:23,164
Reporters came looking into them too,

487
00:28:23,164 --> 00:28:26,216
but there was nothing to find,
so nothing ever came of it.

488
00:28:29,649 --> 00:28:30,649
<i>Breaking news.</i>

489
00:28:30,649 --> 00:28:32,099
[Kingfisher Casino Case Victim]
<i>The full extent of the hidden crimes</i>

490
00:28:32,099 --> 00:28:33,549
[Chairman Cheon's Crimes Revealed]
<i>of Chairman Cheon,</i>

491
00:28:33,549 --> 00:28:36,156
- <i>the casino case victim, once known as</i>
- Sir, look at that!

492
00:28:36,156 --> 00:28:39,029
- <i>Kingfisher's first civilian victim,</i>
- Huh? Turn it up a bit.

493
00:28:39,029 --> 00:28:40,208
<i>has now been revealed.</i>

494
00:28:40,208 --> 00:28:44,512
<i>Chairman Cheon repeatedly sexually assaulted
the wife of a construction worker</i>

495
00:28:44,512 --> 00:28:46,248
<i>after hiring her as a housekeeper.</i>

496
00:28:46,248 --> 00:28:48,124
- <i>When her husband found out</i>
- Oh, my!

497
00:28:48,124 --> 00:28:49,816
<i>and threatened to report him to the police,</i>

498
00:28:49,816 --> 00:28:53,232
<i>Cheon bribed a fellow worker with money
and had the husband murdered</i>

499
00:28:53,232 --> 00:28:54,328
- <i>through contract killing.</i>
- That, that...

500
00:28:54,328 --> 00:28:56,388
- <i>These facts were revealed directly</i>
- What is that?

501
00:28:56,388 --> 00:28:57,749
<i>by the wife of the murdered worker.</i>

502
00:28:57,749 --> 00:29:02,016
<i>This is expected to put to rest claims
that Kingfisher had killed</i>

503
00:29:02,016 --> 00:29:03,960
[Chairman Cheon, Kingfisher Target,]
<i>an innocent civilian for the first time.</i>

504
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:05,556
[Accused of Sexual Assault, Murder-for-Hire]
<i>Police are verifying the report</i>

505
00:29:05,556 --> 00:29:07,584
[Investigative Reporting Team Reporter]
<i>while launching an internal investigation</i>

506
00:29:07,584 --> 00:29:10,816
[Gu Hae Na]
<i>into additional criminal allegations</i>

507
00:29:10,816 --> 00:29:12,349
- <i>involving Chairman Cheon.</i>
- Gu Hae Na!

508
00:29:12,349 --> 00:29:13,652
<i>In our broadcast, Kingfisher...</i>

509
00:29:13,652 --> 00:29:16,768
Ms. Gu, congratulations.
This is a huge scoop.

510
00:29:16,768 --> 00:29:18,616
Yes, thank you.

511
00:29:18,616 --> 00:29:20,149
[Investigative Reporting Team]

512
00:29:20,149 --> 00:29:22,160
Ms. Gu!

513
00:29:22,160 --> 00:29:24,904
Is it really okay for a rookie
to land an exclusive this quickly?

514
00:29:24,904 --> 00:29:26,312
You're going to make the seniors look bad.

515
00:29:26,312 --> 00:29:27,780
You owe us a treat. You have to treat us.

516
00:29:27,780 --> 00:29:31,304
- Actually, it's not my exclusive...
- What do you mean?

517
00:29:31,304 --> 00:29:34,432
How did we have such a talented person
at our company without knowing?

518
00:29:34,432 --> 00:29:36,376
How on earth did you scoop this?

519
00:29:36,376 --> 00:29:40,916
Actually, I wasn't the one who got it...

520
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,308
She says she'll treat us, Chief.

521
00:29:43,308 --> 00:29:45,392
Come on, don't squeeze a rookie dry.

522
00:29:45,392 --> 00:29:48,416
Still, she should treat us all.
It's her first exclusive.

523
00:29:48,416 --> 00:29:52,316
[Chairman Cheon, Kingfisher Target,
Accused of Sexual Assault, Murder-for-Hire]

524
00:29:52,316 --> 00:29:53,683
[Investigative Reporting Team Reporter,
Gu Hae Na]

525
00:29:53,683 --> 00:29:56,616
[Related Articles]

526
00:30:10,404 --> 00:30:14,416
She wants to move up the final meeting.

527
00:30:15,056 --> 00:30:16,708
If possible, right away today.

528
00:30:16,708 --> 00:30:17,816
Today, right away?

529
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:19,072
"Feint east, strike west."

530
00:30:19,072 --> 00:30:21,476
"Make noise in the east
and strike in the west."

531
00:30:21,476 --> 00:30:23,183
Where is Tae Min?

532
00:30:38,448 --> 00:30:40,188
When was the last time you washed your hair?

533
00:30:40,188 --> 00:30:43,272
Do you even wash your clothes?
Do you ever change your socks?

534
00:30:43,272 --> 00:30:45,883
At least wear shoes!

535
00:30:48,416 --> 00:30:50,816
Have you no consideration for your partner?

536
00:30:50,816 --> 00:30:54,524
Your hair's greasy, your clothes
are filthy, and your shoes stink.

537
00:30:54,524 --> 00:30:58,249
At this rate, I'll suffocate
before the meeting even starts!

538
00:31:04,732 --> 00:31:07,449
What... What are you doing?

539
00:31:12,636 --> 00:31:14,649
It was here.

540
00:31:15,664 --> 00:31:17,716
Darn it.

541
00:31:20,824 --> 00:31:24,744
This isn't the kind of scene I dreamed of.

542
00:31:24,744 --> 00:31:28,416
My dream was to someday
stand side by side with Kingfisher...

543
00:31:57,584 --> 00:31:59,740
He ordered a lot.

544
00:31:59,740 --> 00:32:01,449
Looks good.

545
00:32:14,268 --> 00:32:17,816
Oh, I'm starving. I'm starving.

546
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:22,549
Alright, let's see.

547
00:32:23,228 --> 00:32:26,436
Sweet and sour pork,
pepper and veggie stir-fry,

548
00:32:26,436 --> 00:32:29,849
jjajangmyeon, jjajangmyeon...

549
00:32:32,684 --> 00:32:36,272
The punk who burned his own parents alive
sure has an appetite.

550
00:32:36,272 --> 00:32:38,049
Unbelievable.

551
00:32:38,049 --> 00:32:39,754
Does it make sense that he only got six years

552
00:32:39,754 --> 00:32:41,288
for burning his parents alive
for their inheritance?

553
00:32:41,288 --> 00:32:44,236
Claim diminished mental capacity
and write fifty apology letters a day.

554
00:32:44,236 --> 00:32:45,764
Who doesn't know that?

555
00:32:45,764 --> 00:32:48,240
That punk's all lies...

556
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:49,940
Huh?

557
00:32:50,716 --> 00:32:52,883
- Ah, that darn fly.
- <i>Over to Kim Gyeong Ho.</i>

558
00:32:52,883 --> 00:32:54,576
<i>He gets it. Shoot!</i>

559
00:32:54,576 --> 00:32:56,276
<i>This is...</i>

560
00:33:05,172 --> 00:33:06,483
<i>Opposite side!</i>

561
00:33:06,483 --> 00:33:08,549
<i>Layup!</i>

562
00:33:08,549 --> 00:33:10,552
Darn it.

563
00:33:10,552 --> 00:33:12,056
Hey!

564
00:33:12,056 --> 00:33:13,149
Darn it, what?

565
00:33:13,149 --> 00:33:14,324
What?

566
00:33:14,324 --> 00:33:16,240
- <i>Now, he's running.</i>
- What happened?

567
00:33:16,240 --> 00:33:18,064
That's right, that's right!

568
00:33:18,064 --> 00:33:21,579
Oh, darn it!

569
00:33:27,024 --> 00:33:29,280
It's 10 milliliters of concentrated Mist S.

570
00:33:29,280 --> 00:33:31,872
Its casing is water-soluble,
so it dissolves on contact with water

571
00:33:31,872 --> 00:33:33,392
<i>and causes death within five minutes.</i>

572
00:33:33,392 --> 00:33:36,872
It breaks down within an hour,
so it won't show up even in an autopsy.

573
00:33:36,872 --> 00:33:38,520
<i>Ten seconds remaining.</i>

574
00:33:38,520 --> 00:33:42,372
Oh, there's not much time left. Hurry up!

575
00:33:42,372 --> 00:33:43,396
<i>Now, the remaining time.</i>

576
00:33:43,396 --> 00:33:46,004
<i>5 seconds, 4 seconds,</i>

577
00:33:46,004 --> 00:33:50,035
<i>3 seconds, 2 seconds, 1 second.</i>

578
00:33:50,035 --> 00:33:51,592
<i>He shoots!</i>

579
00:33:51,592 --> 00:33:53,249
<i>Beyond the 3-point line!</i>

580
00:33:53,249 --> 00:33:56,024
<i>Is it in? Is it going in?</i>

581
00:33:56,024 --> 00:33:57,644
<i>It's in!</i>

582
00:33:57,644 --> 00:34:00,649
- Yes!
- <i>Three-point buzzer-beater! Good!</i>

583
00:34:04,228 --> 00:34:06,249
<i>That wins the game!</i>

584
00:34:06,249 --> 00:34:09,956
- Hey, you had it in you.
- <i>What a way to finish the game.</i>

585
00:34:09,956 --> 00:34:11,588
Hey, you should've played like that
from the start.

586
00:34:11,588 --> 00:34:14,249
<i>Looks like they're ready for the playoffs.</i>

587
00:34:28,348 --> 00:34:30,048
Meeting clear.

588
00:34:30,048 --> 00:34:31,816
Nice!

589
00:35:01,692 --> 00:35:03,716
Rest in peace.

590
00:35:05,064 --> 00:35:08,949
If you see your parents,
make sure you apologize to them.

591
00:35:10,748 --> 00:35:12,716
That punk.

592
00:35:19,256 --> 00:35:22,464
We wrapped up our final meeting,

593
00:35:22,464 --> 00:35:24,600
so let's have a team dinner for once.

594
00:35:24,600 --> 00:35:27,284
How about beef? Let's have beef.

595
00:35:27,284 --> 00:35:30,936
This month's operating expenses
have been settled too.

596
00:35:30,936 --> 00:35:32,588
Oh, really?

597
00:35:32,588 --> 00:35:35,176
All right, then how about beef? Huh?

598
00:35:35,176 --> 00:35:36,740
Let's have beef, okay?

599
00:35:36,740 --> 00:35:39,783
How about beef? Let's have beef!

600
00:35:43,140 --> 00:35:45,816
<i>Yul going missing isn't your fault.</i>

601
00:35:46,432 --> 00:35:49,683
<i>So please don't cry. I'll find her for you.</i>

602
00:36:08,083 --> 00:36:11,356
<i>If you keep thinking about someone all day</i>

603
00:36:11,356 --> 00:36:14,024
<i>and smile every time they cross your mind,</i>

604
00:36:14,024 --> 00:36:16,992
<i>is that love?</i>

605
00:36:16,992 --> 00:36:18,692
[Mr. Tiger]
<i>Busy.</i>

606
00:36:19,416 --> 00:36:22,649
<i>I think I'm falling in love.</i>

607
00:36:24,449 --> 00:36:27,316
[Mr. Tiger]
<i>Hehe...</i>

608
00:36:27,316 --> 00:36:29,049
Jeez...

609
00:36:31,288 --> 00:36:34,516
<i>Forget it. What would you know about love?</i>

610
00:36:34,516 --> 00:36:35,783
<i>You're a lifelong single. What do you know?</i>

611
00:36:35,783 --> 00:36:37,516
And what about you?

612
00:36:41,152 --> 00:36:42,788
<i>Then tell me what to do.</i>

613
00:36:42,788 --> 00:36:45,616
<i>I've never felt this way before.
I don't know what to do.</i>

614
00:36:47,896 --> 00:36:49,564
<i>Just ask him to meet.</i>

615
00:36:49,564 --> 00:36:52,783
<i>You have to meet him before you can
even get rejected. Hehe...</i>

616
00:36:54,088 --> 00:36:56,236
<i>Is that really okay?</i>

617
00:36:56,236 --> 00:36:58,883
<i>Or just find a natural excuse to see him.</i>

618
00:37:00,784 --> 00:37:02,484
<i>How?</i>

619
00:37:03,492 --> 00:37:05,192
<i>Busy.</i>

620
00:37:06,664 --> 00:37:08,816
He doesn't know either.

621
00:37:11,183 --> 00:37:14,616
A natural excuse to meet?

622
00:37:23,292 --> 00:37:25,516
Oh, seriously...

623
00:37:33,072 --> 00:37:34,640
Se Ah, what brings you here at this hour?

624
00:37:34,640 --> 00:37:36,224
I came to see Yul!

625
00:37:36,224 --> 00:37:37,268
Auntie!

626
00:37:37,268 --> 00:37:40,364
- Looks so delicious.
- Sangju dried persimmons, Yul's favorite.

627
00:37:40,364 --> 00:37:43,968
Open wide! Here we go! Whoosh!

628
00:37:43,968 --> 00:37:46,496
- Wider! Say, "Ah!"
- "Ah!"

629
00:37:46,496 --> 00:37:49,064
Commander, that's not
the right route. Rerouting.

630
00:37:49,064 --> 00:37:52,144
No, not this way. I don't want to eat it.

631
00:37:52,144 --> 00:37:53,996
- Oh, my.
- Daddy!

632
00:37:53,996 --> 00:37:55,740
Yum, it's good!

633
00:37:55,740 --> 00:37:57,440
Yul, say "Ah!"

634
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:01,356
- Yum, it's good!
- It's good, right?

635
00:38:01,356 --> 00:38:03,644
Eat up.

636
00:38:03,644 --> 00:38:06,952
Bo Na, work must be really
tough for you lately, right?

637
00:38:06,952 --> 00:38:09,783
Not really. He's been helping me a lot,
so I'm doing fine.

638
00:38:09,783 --> 00:38:11,104
And I have a reliable sister-in-law too.

639
00:38:11,104 --> 00:38:14,016
Oh, I haven't done anything.

640
00:38:14,884 --> 00:38:16,236
Se Ah, did you come
because you need pocket money?

641
00:38:16,236 --> 00:38:17,928
No.

642
00:38:17,928 --> 00:38:21,144
How are things with your coworkers?
Are they treating you well?

643
00:38:21,144 --> 00:38:24,808
They've been really helpful,
so I've adjusted without much trouble.

644
00:38:24,808 --> 00:38:28,652
Oh, they must all be wonderful people.

645
00:38:28,652 --> 00:38:32,752
Tae Seong, shouldn't you treat them
to a meal sometime?

646
00:38:32,752 --> 00:38:34,412
- All of a sudden?
- Bo Na,

647
00:38:34,412 --> 00:38:37,883
since you got married,
have you ever had a housewarming party?

648
00:38:38,896 --> 00:38:40,396
A housewarming party?

649
00:38:40,396 --> 00:38:43,349
Inviting those people over,
showing them the house,

650
00:38:43,349 --> 00:38:45,136
and serving them food, that kind of thing.

651
00:38:45,136 --> 00:38:47,883
No, I've never really thought about it.

652
00:38:51,315 --> 00:38:52,780
Tae Seong, don't you know that nowadays,

653
00:38:52,780 --> 00:38:54,968
a husband's support
is just as important as a wife's?

654
00:38:54,968 --> 00:38:57,728
Working moms already
have enough pressure at work.

655
00:38:57,728 --> 00:39:02,049
You need to take care of things
so work is easier for her, right?

656
00:39:04,324 --> 00:39:06,292
You've got a point.

657
00:39:06,292 --> 00:39:08,587
Bo Na, they've been so supportive of you

658
00:39:08,587 --> 00:39:11,308
since you returned to work after three years,

659
00:39:11,308 --> 00:39:14,876
so why not show your appreciation
by treating them to a nice home-cooked meal?

660
00:39:14,876 --> 00:39:18,100
That's what makes life feel warm and fun.

661
00:39:18,100 --> 00:39:21,575
Think of it as a company dinner! Huh?

662
00:39:21,575 --> 00:39:23,316
A company dinner?

663
00:39:27,549 --> 00:39:34,016
Why would Director Yoo summon us
to her home herself?

664
00:39:34,708 --> 00:39:37,483
She's never really had people over before.

665
00:39:38,796 --> 00:39:42,008
Maybe it's some kind of cover
to avoid drawing attention?

666
00:39:42,008 --> 00:39:45,224
Our Director Yoo isn't exactly the type
to put on an act like that, okay?

667
00:39:45,224 --> 00:39:47,456
What should we bring as a gift?

668
00:39:47,456 --> 00:39:50,132
Nothing beats toilet paper.
May everything go smoothly.

669
00:39:50,132 --> 00:39:53,536
Come on, diffusers are the trend these days.

670
00:39:53,536 --> 00:39:55,340
How about a wine glass set?

671
00:39:55,340 --> 00:39:58,016
Booze is better than glasses.

672
00:39:59,724 --> 00:40:02,900
But is Manager Tae Min not coming with us?

673
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:05,056
Manager Tae doesn't really go out
unless it's for a meeting.

674
00:40:05,056 --> 00:40:07,104
He's a total homebody.

675
00:40:07,104 --> 00:40:10,883
Yeah, he'd probably just be a burden.
Especially since she's got kids at home.

676
00:40:11,548 --> 00:40:14,132
How about a nice mood lamp?

677
00:40:14,132 --> 00:40:15,832
A mood lamp?

678
00:40:17,240 --> 00:40:19,500
Let's keep it simple.

679
00:40:19,500 --> 00:40:21,749
You know what I mean, right?

680
00:40:22,496 --> 00:40:24,649
My favorite wine.

681
00:40:26,912 --> 00:40:29,216
- Okay.
- So you'd already made up your mind.

682
00:40:29,888 --> 00:40:32,349
- Pork belly and ribs are on sale today.
- Oh, ribs!

683
00:40:32,349 --> 00:40:33,841
- Have a look.
- Okay.

684
00:40:33,841 --> 00:40:36,340
- How about this?
- Pork belly and short ribs are on sale.

685
00:40:36,340 --> 00:40:38,204
It's huge, right?

686
00:40:38,204 --> 00:40:39,569
Alright.

687
00:40:39,569 --> 00:40:41,381
There we go.

688
00:40:44,380 --> 00:40:47,283
What is next?

689
00:40:47,888 --> 00:40:51,816
Frozen pollock and two mackerel, right?

690
00:40:52,828 --> 00:40:55,249
- Let's go.
- Mommy, squid!

691
00:40:55,249 --> 00:40:57,449
Should we get squid now?

692
00:40:57,449 --> 00:40:58,832
Veggies, veggies!

693
00:40:58,832 --> 00:41:00,328
Huh? Should we get veggies now?

694
00:41:00,328 --> 00:41:02,649
Okay, we can get veggies now.

695
00:41:03,644 --> 00:41:04,716
What was next after that?

696
00:41:04,716 --> 00:41:07,014
Wow, look at that cart.

697
00:41:07,014 --> 00:41:10,083
She is really excited.

698
00:41:11,672 --> 00:41:13,612
We should've done this sooner.

699
00:41:13,612 --> 00:41:15,876
But when I think about it,
she's really something.

700
00:41:15,876 --> 00:41:19,284
There's so much she's never done,
and so much she's never experienced.

701
00:41:19,284 --> 00:41:22,215
How on earth has she lived her life?

702
00:41:22,215 --> 00:41:23,256
Do you know anything about it?

703
00:41:23,256 --> 00:41:24,956
Huh?

704
00:41:26,516 --> 00:41:29,549
I'm her husband. How would I not know?

705
00:41:30,424 --> 00:41:32,601
You clearly don't!

706
00:41:32,601 --> 00:41:34,420
Bo Na!

707
00:41:34,420 --> 00:41:36,683
Tae Seong, go grab a cart. A cart.

708
00:41:36,683 --> 00:41:38,549
- Okay.
- Bo Na!

709
00:41:38,549 --> 00:41:39,549
Yeah, Se Ah.

710
00:41:39,549 --> 00:41:40,584
Hold onto this for a second.

711
00:41:40,584 --> 00:41:41,784
Huh?

712
00:41:41,784 --> 00:41:43,728
Oh, well... Bo Na.

713
00:41:43,728 --> 00:41:46,616
The hacker who came
to the playground that time...

714
00:41:47,751 --> 00:41:49,216
I mean, your colleague.

715
00:41:49,216 --> 00:41:51,312
Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do?

716
00:41:51,312 --> 00:41:54,600
So his name is Ki Yeong Do.

717
00:41:54,600 --> 00:41:56,540
What a good name...

718
00:41:56,540 --> 00:41:59,083
Oh, don't worry.

719
00:42:00,136 --> 00:42:01,836
Thank you.

720
00:42:03,152 --> 00:42:08,216
Do you know what kind of food he likes?

721
00:42:09,218 --> 00:42:10,918
I'm not sure.

722
00:42:11,609 --> 00:42:12,880
Oh, well...

723
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:18,284
Since he helped us so much
in finding Yul, so... to repay him!

724
00:42:18,284 --> 00:42:22,868
Wouldn't it be nice to include
at least one side dish he likes

725
00:42:22,868 --> 00:42:25,852
as a small token of gratitude?

726
00:42:25,852 --> 00:42:27,783
Now that you mention it, you're right.

727
00:42:27,783 --> 00:42:29,483
What should we make?

728
00:42:30,304 --> 00:42:31,776
He's a picky eater, though.

729
00:42:31,776 --> 00:42:34,992
Oh, he's a light eater.

730
00:42:34,992 --> 00:42:40,148
Still, his hand keeps going back to it,
that kind of thing?

731
00:42:49,372 --> 00:42:50,568
Oh! Hello!

732
00:42:50,568 --> 00:42:53,164
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

733
00:42:53,164 --> 00:42:55,324
- Shall we go in?
- Yeah, please come in.

734
00:42:55,324 --> 00:42:57,249
- Let's see.
- Excuse us.

735
00:42:58,224 --> 00:42:59,224
What a nice place, right?

736
00:42:59,224 --> 00:43:00,924
Yeah.

737
00:43:01,620 --> 00:43:02,916
- Come on in.
- Okay.

738
00:43:02,916 --> 00:43:04,740
Please come in. Honey!

739
00:43:04,740 --> 00:43:05,740
- Yeah.
- They're here.

740
00:43:05,740 --> 00:43:07,996
You're here?

741
00:43:07,996 --> 00:43:10,716
Thanks for coming all this way.

742
00:43:12,040 --> 00:43:14,372
This is my husband, Kwon Tae Seong.

743
00:43:14,372 --> 00:43:15,876
Nice to meet you.

744
00:43:15,876 --> 00:43:19,044
I should've invited you over sooner.
I feel like it's so late.

745
00:43:19,044 --> 00:43:20,708
Thank you so much for coming.

746
00:43:20,708 --> 00:43:24,061
We're the ones who should be thanking you
for inviting us into your home.

747
00:43:24,061 --> 00:43:25,240
Oh, not at all.

748
00:43:25,240 --> 00:43:29,316
Oh, my, your husband is so handsome.

749
00:43:31,312 --> 00:43:32,616
Really?

750
00:43:32,616 --> 00:43:34,276
Yul, say hello.

751
00:43:34,276 --> 00:43:35,760
They're Mommy's friends from work.

752
00:43:35,760 --> 00:43:37,004
Hello.

753
00:43:37,004 --> 00:43:39,883
- Hello.
- So you're Yul?

754
00:43:39,883 --> 00:43:41,992
Mind if we look around?

755
00:43:41,992 --> 00:43:43,720
- Of course, go ahead.
- Sure, make yourselves at home.

756
00:43:43,720 --> 00:43:45,052
Yes, make yourselves at home. Please come in.

757
00:43:45,052 --> 00:43:46,652
Why did you bring so much?

758
00:43:46,652 --> 00:43:48,332
- It's all for you, Director Yoo.
- You can definitely tell

759
00:43:48,332 --> 00:43:50,651
a child lives here.

760
00:43:50,651 --> 00:43:52,383
It's so cozy and cute.

761
00:43:53,192 --> 00:43:54,868
Half the stuff is for the baby.

762
00:43:54,868 --> 00:43:57,056
Finally, I get to see it.

763
00:43:57,056 --> 00:44:00,624
I was really curious
what it looked like inside.

764
00:44:00,624 --> 00:44:04,016
Mommy! Auntie Se Ah became a princess!

765
00:44:07,880 --> 00:44:09,580
Oh, really?

766
00:44:13,092 --> 00:44:15,528
This is my youngest sister.

767
00:44:15,528 --> 00:44:19,016
She came by to help out today.

768
00:44:19,648 --> 00:44:22,460
Your sister even helped
with the housewarming party?

769
00:44:22,460 --> 00:44:24,616
That's so sweet of her.

770
00:44:25,516 --> 00:44:27,483
Nice to meet you.

771
00:44:27,483 --> 00:44:29,883
I'm Kwon Se Ah.

772
00:44:33,656 --> 00:44:35,356
Honey.

773
00:44:36,888 --> 00:44:38,588
Have you been drinking?

774
00:44:42,084 --> 00:44:44,824
- Wow!
- Oh, my, the table's going to collapse.

775
00:44:44,824 --> 00:44:47,596
You didn't make all this yourself, did you?

776
00:44:47,596 --> 00:44:50,974
Wait, you're saying you made
this entire feast yourself?

777
00:44:50,974 --> 00:44:53,603
- Well...
- I was going to order some of it,

778
00:44:53,603 --> 00:44:55,892
but she insisted on
making everything herself.

779
00:44:55,892 --> 00:44:58,324
I made it all.

780
00:44:58,324 --> 00:45:01,664
They say a housewarming meal
should be made with care,

781
00:45:01,664 --> 00:45:04,632
so I put my heart into it.

782
00:45:04,632 --> 00:45:08,316
This is a classic festive dish made with
glass noodles, meat, and vegetables,

783
00:45:08,316 --> 00:45:11,252
all beautifully combined.

784
00:45:11,252 --> 00:45:15,224
It's a hearty meat dish
that's perfect for serving guests.

785
00:45:15,224 --> 00:45:19,908
And these pancakes, easy to eat,
but you can feel the effort put into them.

786
00:45:19,908 --> 00:45:22,092
I made it all myself.

787
00:45:22,092 --> 00:45:25,048
Well, since I came back,

788
00:45:25,048 --> 00:45:29,183
you've all helped me so much to readjust.
I'm really grateful.

789
00:45:31,040 --> 00:45:35,483
I really wanted to make you all
a warm, home-cooked meal.

790
00:45:36,404 --> 00:45:40,520
I've been wanting to say this for a while.

791
00:45:40,520 --> 00:45:42,316
There's not much, but please eat your fill.

792
00:45:42,316 --> 00:45:44,848
Oh, come on.

793
00:45:44,848 --> 00:45:47,216
Look at all this food.

794
00:45:47,216 --> 00:45:49,008
I think we're really going to feast today.

795
00:45:49,008 --> 00:45:50,320
Eat plenty.

796
00:45:50,320 --> 00:45:51,816
Thank you for the meal!

797
00:45:51,816 --> 00:45:53,949
- Thank you for the meal!
- Thank you.

798
00:45:53,949 --> 00:45:55,683
Come on, dig in.

799
00:45:56,336 --> 00:45:58,583
- Enjoy your meal.
- Yeah, thanks.

800
00:46:03,504 --> 00:46:07,096
I heard from my sister-in-law
that you sometimes enjoy this,

801
00:46:07,096 --> 00:46:11,983
so I made some.

802
00:46:12,616 --> 00:46:14,516
I hope you enjoy it.

803
00:46:15,836 --> 00:46:17,780
Eat up, Se Ah.

804
00:46:17,780 --> 00:46:19,432
Want some short ribs?

805
00:46:19,432 --> 00:46:20,536
- Yeah!
- I'll cut it for you.

806
00:46:20,536 --> 00:46:21,559
- It's good.
- Honey, I'll do it.

807
00:46:21,559 --> 00:46:23,836
- You didn't even have lunch.
- Honey, eat a lot.

808
00:46:23,836 --> 00:46:26,072
Honey, want some of that?

809
00:46:26,072 --> 00:46:29,048
You two are so sweet.

810
00:46:29,048 --> 00:46:32,883
Can I ask how you two first met?

811
00:46:34,196 --> 00:46:36,952
We just...

812
00:46:36,952 --> 00:46:39,810
met like that, coming and going.

813
00:46:39,810 --> 00:46:42,684
Actually, a pickpocket brought us together.

814
00:46:42,684 --> 00:46:44,083
- A pickpocket?
- Yeah.

815
00:46:44,083 --> 00:46:46,632
About eight years ago,
I was covering a pickpocketing case

816
00:46:46,632 --> 00:46:48,192
and suffered a serious head injury.

817
00:46:48,192 --> 00:46:52,164
Oh, goodness. So you went through
quite a terrible ordeal.

818
00:46:52,164 --> 00:46:58,556
But luckily, a woman called an ambulance,
and I barely survived.

819
00:46:58,556 --> 00:47:00,568
The doctors said things could've
turned out much worse

820
00:47:00,568 --> 00:47:02,949
if she'd called even a little later.

821
00:47:03,668 --> 00:47:07,124
After about four months, when I finally
woke up and was able to walk again,

822
00:47:07,124 --> 00:47:11,880
I went up to the hospital rooftop,
and that's where I met Bo Na.

823
00:47:11,880 --> 00:47:16,252
- <i>That day, I fell for Bo Na's bright smile</i>
- Come down!

824
00:47:16,252 --> 00:47:18,812
- at first sight.
- Yes.

825
00:47:18,812 --> 00:47:21,283
How romantic!

826
00:47:21,283 --> 00:47:25,816
I didn't know you two had such a love story.

827
00:47:25,816 --> 00:47:29,148
That's so touching. A love that began
on the boundary between life and death.

828
00:47:29,148 --> 00:47:31,144
Oh, right.

829
00:47:31,144 --> 00:47:36,906
Do you happen to know who the woman was
who called an ambulance back then?

830
00:47:36,906 --> 00:47:40,756
Actually, as soon as I woke up,
I checked with the emergency call center,

831
00:47:40,756 --> 00:47:44,084
but the call was made from my phone,
so I couldn't get her contact info.

832
00:47:44,084 --> 00:47:46,332
And they couldn't remember
anything about the caller

833
00:47:46,332 --> 00:47:48,520
other than that she was a woman.

834
00:47:48,520 --> 00:47:52,349
But she'll probably be greatly blessed.

835
00:47:52,349 --> 00:47:55,304
She saved your life. Don't you think?

836
00:47:55,304 --> 00:47:58,284
Then wasn't it that woman,
rather than the pickpocket,

837
00:47:58,284 --> 00:48:00,983
who brought you two together?

838
00:48:02,588 --> 00:48:04,459
Now that she mentions it, that's true.

839
00:48:04,459 --> 00:48:08,216
I should find her somehow
and thank her, right?

840
00:48:08,216 --> 00:48:09,860
- You should.
- Yes, I'll do it.

841
00:48:09,860 --> 00:48:12,516
It's getting cold. Please eat up.

842
00:48:13,728 --> 00:48:16,483
Well... Assistant Manager Ki.

843
00:48:17,096 --> 00:48:19,520
You should try some meat too.

844
00:48:19,520 --> 00:48:21,868
Here... Oh, my.

845
00:48:21,868 --> 00:48:22,868
Oh, no!

846
00:48:22,868 --> 00:48:25,512
Hold on, let me...

847
00:48:25,512 --> 00:48:27,528
Oh, what do I do? Wet wipes.

848
00:48:27,528 --> 00:48:29,524
I'm so sorry, Assistant Manager Ki.

849
00:48:29,524 --> 00:48:31,072
It's okay.

850
00:48:31,072 --> 00:48:32,624
Do you have any cold beer?

851
00:48:32,624 --> 00:48:33,624
Beer?

852
00:48:33,624 --> 00:48:36,516
Sure, I'll get you one right away.

853
00:48:37,552 --> 00:48:39,584
Here.

854
00:48:39,584 --> 00:48:41,716
Let me open it for you.

855
00:49:01,744 --> 00:49:03,444
At least have this...

856
00:49:13,983 --> 00:49:15,656
[Eight Years Ago, Spring]

857
00:49:15,656 --> 00:49:18,704
[Personnel Profile]
I never applied for a job at this company.

858
00:49:18,704 --> 00:49:19,940
There must be some mistake...

859
00:49:19,940 --> 00:49:25,004
You must've been surprised to suddenly
receive a job application by email.

860
00:49:25,004 --> 00:49:27,616
You were kidnapped as a child.

861
00:49:27,616 --> 00:49:31,549
You majored in psychology,
and your specialty is hacking, huh?

862
00:49:34,092 --> 00:49:36,583
Durumi Electronics, Sales Team 3.

863
00:49:37,376 --> 00:49:40,349
It seems like they do different work
from other departments.

864
00:49:47,604 --> 00:49:48,652
Go on.

865
00:49:48,652 --> 00:49:52,740
The sales records look subtly
different from those of other departments.

866
00:49:52,740 --> 00:49:56,116
It felt like they'd taken real data
and pieced it together, you know?

867
00:49:56,116 --> 00:49:58,576
The fieldwork ratio
in the work logs is unusual too.

868
00:49:58,576 --> 00:50:02,968
So did you figure out what they actually do?

869
00:50:02,968 --> 00:50:07,049
Only that it's illegal?

870
00:50:08,096 --> 00:50:10,044
That's right.

871
00:50:10,044 --> 00:50:14,683
Sales Team 3 selects
and eliminates criminals.

872
00:50:16,592 --> 00:50:20,508
For several reasons,
I like your qualifications, Mr. Ki Yeong Do.

873
00:50:20,508 --> 00:50:23,249
What happens if I turn you down?

874
00:50:25,840 --> 00:50:29,316
We only make offers to people
who won't refuse.

875
00:50:30,156 --> 00:50:34,083
And if I still refuse, will I be killed?

876
00:50:39,740 --> 00:50:42,016
Then you'll have to keep our secret.

877
00:50:50,532 --> 00:50:53,983
What are you going to do?
Will you keep the secret?

878
00:50:58,956 --> 00:51:00,749
You scared?

879
00:51:15,388 --> 00:51:17,683
Eat up and relax, rookie.

880
00:51:25,912 --> 00:51:29,183
This is the best cure for stress. Eat.

881
00:51:53,032 --> 00:51:57,483
I'm done. I'm done.

882
00:51:58,156 --> 00:52:01,136
Ugh, just get out of here.

883
00:52:01,136 --> 00:52:03,149
Just go out and die.

884
00:52:07,849 --> 00:52:09,628
Look at this.

885
00:52:09,628 --> 00:52:11,583
Wow!

886
00:52:11,583 --> 00:52:13,084
- Oh, dear.
- Yul.

887
00:52:13,084 --> 00:52:15,336
Want some strawberries?

888
00:52:15,336 --> 00:52:17,376
- Let's all raise our glasses.
- Cheers!

889
00:52:17,376 --> 00:52:20,656
I'm sorry for causing a scene.

890
00:52:20,656 --> 00:52:22,776
I'm going to head home first.

891
00:52:22,776 --> 00:52:23,776
- Where are you going?
- Perfect.

892
00:52:23,776 --> 00:52:27,120
Assistant Manager Ki is heading home,
so you can walk him to the main road.

893
00:52:27,120 --> 00:52:29,052
He's taking the subway, so take him out
through the back entrance.

894
00:52:29,052 --> 00:52:31,116
- Me?
- Yeah.

895
00:52:31,116 --> 00:52:32,116
- Why?
- What do you mean, why?

896
00:52:32,116 --> 00:52:34,456
He doesn't know the way.

897
00:52:34,456 --> 00:52:37,316
Oh, yeah. Go ahead.

898
00:52:37,316 --> 00:52:38,984
We'll stay a little longer.

899
00:52:38,984 --> 00:52:41,146
- Alright.
- Please eat.

900
00:52:41,146 --> 00:52:42,983
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

901
00:52:44,208 --> 00:52:46,088
Well, Assistant Manager Ki!

902
00:52:46,088 --> 00:52:49,804
I'll make sure to wash your clothes
and return them.

903
00:52:49,804 --> 00:52:51,504
Please do.

904
00:52:52,620 --> 00:52:55,160
Are you very upset?

905
00:52:55,160 --> 00:52:56,860
I'm not happy.

906
00:52:57,848 --> 00:52:59,264
I guess you're pretty upset.

907
00:52:59,264 --> 00:53:01,583
It's because of me...

908
00:53:13,612 --> 00:53:15,816
Does your brother not have hands?

909
00:53:16,664 --> 00:53:18,364
Hands?

910
00:53:22,848 --> 00:53:24,548
Hands?

911
00:53:31,716 --> 00:53:34,049
When will you return my clothes?

912
00:53:35,448 --> 00:53:37,549
Soon? Yeah...

913
00:53:39,472 --> 00:53:43,516
The day you return my clothes,
let's go on a date.

914
00:53:59,396 --> 00:54:02,849
A... date?

915
00:54:06,872 --> 00:54:09,616
That was delicious. I'm stuffed.

916
00:54:10,632 --> 00:54:13,732
By the way, we did okay, right?

917
00:54:13,732 --> 00:54:15,983
Yeah, I think we did.

918
00:54:17,616 --> 00:54:19,716
We didn't make any mistakes, right?

919
00:54:20,428 --> 00:54:22,360
I don't think so.

920
00:54:22,360 --> 00:54:24,060
Good.

921
00:54:25,392 --> 00:54:30,216
Honestly, Director Yoo's cooking
isn't that great, right?

922
00:54:34,956 --> 00:54:38,432
Do we really not need to
erase the CCTV footage?

923
00:54:38,432 --> 00:54:40,316
Oh, Team Leader.

924
00:54:40,316 --> 00:54:42,120
We're not here for a meeting today.

925
00:54:42,120 --> 00:54:43,312
Right, right.

926
00:54:43,312 --> 00:54:46,149
Hey, let's keep it normal. Just act normal.

927
00:54:52,188 --> 00:54:53,896
Oh, go on in.

928
00:54:53,896 --> 00:54:55,176
Yeah, yeah.

929
00:54:55,176 --> 00:54:57,149
Thank you.

930
00:55:01,812 --> 00:55:03,512
Excuse me!

931
00:55:04,768 --> 00:55:07,049
I think you dropped something.

932
00:55:09,728 --> 00:55:11,428
Thank you.

933
00:55:12,432 --> 00:55:14,132
Thank you.

934
00:55:23,012 --> 00:55:24,949
Let's all go.

935
00:55:29,984 --> 00:55:31,116
Mr. Lee!

936
00:55:31,116 --> 00:55:32,628
Oh, my princess!

937
00:55:32,628 --> 00:55:35,708
Wow, my princess!

938
00:55:35,708 --> 00:55:39,368
Mr. Lee, have you caught a lot of bad guys?

939
00:55:39,368 --> 00:55:41,104
I caught this many.

940
00:55:41,104 --> 00:55:43,668
Oh, Yul.

941
00:55:43,668 --> 00:55:45,496
Now, stand at attention!

942
00:55:45,496 --> 00:55:48,896
I protect good kids like you, Yul. I'm...

943
00:55:48,896 --> 00:55:50,012
A police officer!

944
00:55:50,012 --> 00:55:52,436
That's right! Good job.

945
00:55:52,436 --> 00:55:53,720
- Let's go.
- You came earlier than expected.

946
00:55:53,720 --> 00:55:54,908
Guess you're not too busy?

947
00:55:54,908 --> 00:55:58,296
Hey, Bo Na is making braised ribs.
What could be more important than that?

948
00:55:58,296 --> 00:56:01,616
- Go play.
- Dong Jin, you're here?

949
00:56:01,616 --> 00:56:03,580
Thanks for inviting me again.

950
00:56:03,580 --> 00:56:05,292
Oh, it's nothing.

951
00:56:05,292 --> 00:56:08,412
Why does she always call you
whenever she cooks something special?

952
00:56:08,412 --> 00:56:10,544
That's becoming a bad habit.

953
00:56:10,544 --> 00:56:15,080
I may be unlucky with friends,
but I sure lucked out with my friend's wife.

954
00:56:15,080 --> 00:56:17,449
Yeah, you should focus on
finding your wife instead.

955
00:56:18,304 --> 00:56:19,812
Please come by more often.

956
00:56:19,812 --> 00:56:22,912
Yul gets so excited
whenever I tell her you're coming.

957
00:56:22,912 --> 00:56:24,680
Got it. I will.

958
00:56:24,680 --> 00:56:27,548
Anyway, Bo Na, you must be tired
after returning to work.

959
00:56:27,548 --> 00:56:28,583
Does he help you a lot?

960
00:56:28,583 --> 00:56:31,700
He's been so sheltered.
I doubt he knows how to do much.

961
00:56:31,700 --> 00:56:34,232
I'm really good at everything now.

962
00:56:34,232 --> 00:56:36,812
Honey, what else should I do?
Just say the word.

963
00:56:36,812 --> 00:56:39,996
He always means well,
but he's not exactly talented...

964
00:56:39,996 --> 00:56:42,384
Just a moment. I'll go get something for you.

965
00:56:42,384 --> 00:56:45,272
Thank you. I'll repay the favor.

966
00:56:45,272 --> 00:56:47,583
- Sit down, sit down.
- No, it's fine.

967
00:56:48,672 --> 00:56:49,948
Did you have guests over?

968
00:56:49,948 --> 00:56:51,652
Yeah, my wife's coworkers.

969
00:56:51,652 --> 00:56:54,116
They must be the ones who just left.

970
00:56:54,116 --> 00:56:55,340
Did you see them?

971
00:56:55,340 --> 00:56:56,964
Yeah, in front of the elevator
on the first floor.

972
00:56:56,964 --> 00:56:59,483
They seemed really nice.

973
00:57:03,412 --> 00:57:05,196
Looks like I'll be eating
home-cooked meals all week.

974
00:57:05,196 --> 00:57:07,376
Oh, Ms. Bo Na has always...

975
00:57:07,376 --> 00:57:09,508
I helped out with that every time.

976
00:57:09,508 --> 00:57:10,876
You just should say "thank you."

977
00:57:10,876 --> 00:57:14,236
What part? Tell me so I can throw it out.

978
00:57:14,236 --> 00:57:17,649
You said you'd repay the favor. With what?

979
00:57:18,296 --> 00:57:20,048
Do I have money? Do I have connections?

980
00:57:20,048 --> 00:57:22,110
Wow, the ink's barely dry
on your verbal promise,

981
00:57:22,110 --> 00:57:23,288
and you're already like this.

982
00:57:23,288 --> 00:57:27,083
What else can I do but protect? I'm a cop.

983
00:57:28,552 --> 00:57:30,024
Except you, you punk.

984
00:57:30,024 --> 00:57:33,116
I'm only going to protect
your kind wife and pretty Yul.

985
00:57:33,760 --> 00:57:36,683
I'll take care of protecting
my wife and daughter myself.

986
00:57:40,228 --> 00:57:45,056
Make sure you take extra good care of them
on birthdays and holidays.

987
00:57:45,056 --> 00:57:47,183
Not having family

988
00:57:48,028 --> 00:57:51,183
can be terribly lonely and painful.

989
00:58:26,532 --> 00:58:29,752
So what were you curious about?

990
00:58:29,752 --> 00:58:32,404
So you didn't write
the Cheon Seong Gil article after all?

991
00:58:32,404 --> 00:58:34,783
We wrote it together, with a junior reporter.

992
00:58:36,052 --> 00:58:38,000
If you don't want to talk, then that's fine.

993
00:58:38,000 --> 00:58:41,983
Anyway, thanks to that article,
Kingfisher's reputation was saved.

994
00:58:45,044 --> 00:58:48,496
Are you still getting played
by Kingfisher these days?

995
00:58:48,496 --> 00:58:53,183
Man, he's really going all out
since he came back.

996
00:58:53,868 --> 00:58:57,052
He's never operated this tightly before.

997
00:58:57,052 --> 00:58:59,116
If he takes another hiatus,

998
00:58:59,116 --> 00:59:02,064
he'll be back sweeping up
criminals all over the world.

999
00:59:02,064 --> 00:59:04,020
It's the second time.

1000
00:59:04,020 --> 00:59:05,224
- What?
- The hiatus.

1001
00:59:05,224 --> 00:59:07,000
There was one eight years ago, remember?

1002
00:59:07,000 --> 00:59:09,149
After that World Cup incident.

1003
00:59:09,149 --> 00:59:11,176
Oh...

1004
00:59:11,176 --> 00:59:12,349
Was it nine months back then?

1005
00:59:12,349 --> 00:59:14,716
When he came back, everyone was curious too,

1006
00:59:14,716 --> 00:59:16,883
wondering what had happened during that time.

1007
00:59:16,883 --> 00:59:20,336
I know what happened to me during that time.

1008
00:59:20,336 --> 00:59:23,340
I met Yoo Bo Na.

1009
00:59:23,340 --> 00:59:26,932
Were you the one who saved
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong that day?

1010
00:59:26,932 --> 00:59:28,349
<i>Yeah.</i>

1011
00:59:28,349 --> 00:59:29,683
Why?

1012
00:59:29,683 --> 00:59:31,228
Because I wanted to.

1013
00:59:31,228 --> 00:59:33,660
It could have been dangerous.

1014
00:59:33,660 --> 00:59:36,980
It was. Luckily, it wasn't.

1015
00:59:36,980 --> 00:59:39,336
You were secretly glad back then.

1016
00:59:39,336 --> 00:59:42,416
After Kingfisher came back
from the first hiatus.

1017
00:59:42,416 --> 00:59:44,216
I thought you'd feel the same way this time.

1018
00:59:44,216 --> 00:59:49,952
You used to want so badly
to meet Kingfisher. Lost interest now?

1019
00:59:49,952 --> 00:59:51,616
We can't meet.

1020
00:59:51,616 --> 00:59:55,592
<i>What happened after that?</i>

1021
00:59:55,592 --> 00:59:59,268
He... saved me.

1022
00:59:59,268 --> 01:00:01,616
And I came back.

1023
01:00:01,616 --> 01:00:03,160
Then...

1024
01:00:03,160 --> 01:00:05,596
That's right. My husband.

1025
01:00:05,596 --> 01:00:08,216
He's the one who brought me back.

1026
01:00:08,216 --> 01:00:10,249
<i>He shouldn't have come back.</i>

1027
01:00:11,116 --> 01:00:12,296
Not this time...

1028
01:00:12,296 --> 01:00:15,764
And the one who brought me
back as Kingfisher this time...

1029
01:00:15,764 --> 01:00:17,752
He shouldn't have come.

1030
01:00:17,752 --> 01:00:19,676
<i>Kwon Tae Seong,</i>

1031
01:00:19,676 --> 01:00:21,376
it's him.

1032
01:00:25,812 --> 01:00:31,016
It's cold out. How about we
talk about it again when it warms up?

1033
01:00:31,940 --> 01:00:34,360
I've thought about it for a long time.

1034
01:00:34,360 --> 01:00:37,792
I know, but who knows?

1035
01:00:37,792 --> 01:00:41,016
Maybe when the flowers bloom
and spring comes, you'll change your mind.

1036
01:00:44,300 --> 01:00:47,183
I don't want to do anything anymore.

1037
01:00:51,296 --> 01:00:52,700
Take some time off starting today.

1038
01:00:52,700 --> 01:00:55,088
Rest as much as you need.

1039
01:00:55,088 --> 01:00:59,160
Right, this is the perfect time for a trip.

1040
01:00:59,160 --> 01:01:02,580
Anyone have a travel spot
to recommend for Yoo Bo Na?

1041
01:01:02,580 --> 01:01:06,849
Somewhere with mountains, fresh air,
and nothing you have to do.

1042
01:01:08,592 --> 01:01:10,292
That's...

1043
01:01:14,512 --> 01:01:16,044
What about here?

1044
01:01:16,044 --> 01:01:19,672
It's quiet, there's no one around,
and there's no cell service.

1045
01:01:19,672 --> 01:01:22,649
They even serve three meals
a day on schedule.

1046
01:01:24,816 --> 01:01:26,716
Right, a trip should be by the sea.

1047
01:01:26,716 --> 01:01:29,036
Somewhere wide open, right?

1048
01:01:29,036 --> 01:01:31,916
Yeah, you can take a boat. It's perfect.

1049
01:01:31,916 --> 01:01:33,956
- Go there.
- And if you come back

1050
01:01:33,956 --> 01:01:38,532
and still feel the same,
I'll accept your resignation.

1051
01:01:38,532 --> 01:01:40,232
Okay?

1052
01:02:06,060 --> 01:02:09,696
Oh, dear, she's not eating.
I don't know why she's like that.

1053
01:02:09,696 --> 01:02:11,580
Did she skip another meal?

1054
01:02:11,580 --> 01:02:14,749
I'm worried, so worried.

1055
01:04:46,736 --> 01:04:49,008
What do you think of
when you see icicles, Bo Na?

1056
01:04:49,008 --> 01:04:51,540
It'd be perfect for piercing
a vital spot in one go.

1057
01:04:51,540 --> 01:04:54,748
I've never really looked at something
and thought it was pretty.

1058
01:04:54,748 --> 01:04:56,224
I'll show you plenty of beautiful things
from now on.

1059
01:04:56,224 --> 01:04:59,084
They've closed all the roads
into the mountain since yesterday afternoon.

1060
01:04:59,084 --> 01:05:01,183
Looks like we're stranded.

1061
01:05:02,168 --> 01:05:03,884
Bo Na!

1062
01:05:03,884 --> 01:05:05,436
Why did you do that
right after being released?

1063
01:05:05,436 --> 01:05:07,592
Isn't all of this because the police
can't catch Kingfisher?

1064
01:05:07,592 --> 01:05:11,272
To me, Kingfisher is
a psychopath, a murderer.

1065
01:05:11,272 --> 01:05:13,216
You're the family of a crime victim.

1066
01:05:13,216 --> 01:05:15,080
Can I borrow this for the weekend?

1067
01:05:15,080 --> 01:05:16,180
I have something to confess.

1068
01:05:16,180 --> 01:05:19,616
I know... who Kingfisher is.
